    "result_text": "Done. The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` create pipeline needed to emit a welcome notification on successful create \u2014 a line on the `NOTIFY` logger carrying both the owner id and the `memberId`.\n\n**New function step** \u2014 `EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java`:\n```java\nprivate static final Logger NOTIFY = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\");\n\npublic void service(@Val Owner owner) {\n    NOTIFY.info(\"Welcome notification enqueued: id={} memberId={}\",\n            owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n}\n```\n\n**Wired into `owners.POST.yml`** as a new `welcome` step between `record` (idempotency) and `respond`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbours:\n```yaml\nrecord:\n  ...\n  next: welcome\nwelcome:\n  class: ...EnqueueWelcomeNotification\n  govern: [ transaction ]\n  next: respond\n```\n\nPlacing it after `SaveOwner` ensures the generated owner `id` is populated, while `memberId` is already assigned upstream by `AssignMemberId`. It reads the entity via `@Val` (no second `@RequestBody` binding, no extra response), consistent with the project's function-injection conventions.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` test \u2014 which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line containing the owner id and fetched `memberId` \u2014 passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`. The log output confirms the line: `NOTIFY - Welcome notification enqueued: id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`.",
